Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13 (@wu-ufc: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R
U.S. Department of Defense, prepared by NAVFAC with the Army and Air Force. UFC 3-230-13, 1 March 2023. [Complete official manual](https://www.wbdg.org/FFC/DOD/UFC/ufc_3_230_13_2023.pdf).

Read the whole manual for an industrial-service study. Chapters 2–3 establish treatment purposes and makeup-water processes; 4–6 develop steam boilers, cooling and closed systems; 7 addresses sampling and testing. Follow the operating account through the appendices and the equipment's actual requirements. Relate concentration, corrosion, deposits and biological growth to measurements and continuing maintenance.

The inspected PDF has 276 file pages and supersedes UFC 3-240-13FN of 25 May 2005. It is approved for public release and unlimited distribution, with separately identified copyrighted material. Its mandatory criteria belong to its stated DoD context; they are not universal water standards. Preserve the revision and component notices.

